// The game clock and the anchors that pin every calendar to day 0 (GDD §3, ADR-0007).
//
// Times are minutes since the midnight that opens the game day. A day runs
// 05:00 → 01:00, so `dayEndMinute` is past 24:00 (1500 = 01:00 the next morning).
// At 10 sim ticks per second (ARCHITECTURE §3.1), 7 ticks per game minute is the
// GDD's "1 game-minute = 0.7 real s", which makes a day ~14 real minutes.
//
// Day 0 is the arrival and the first day of Kasa. The anchors below are design
// choices, not facts to verify: the real Kasa starts around 22 June, and 22 June
// 2026 was a Senin falling on 6 Muharram 1448 in the tabular calendar, so the
// save opens in a plausible present. Pasaran is `day % 5` (ADR-0007), so day 0
// is Legi by definition.
{
  ticksPerMinute: 7,
  dayStartMinute: 300,
  dayEndMinute: 1500,
  weekdayOfDay0: 'mon',
  hijriOfDay0: { year: 1448, month: 1, day: 6 },
}
